      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason we implement like this because both the INCREMENT_CALL_DEPTH and INCREMENT_CALL_DEPTH_PKVM will be used when CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL\u003dy. INCREMENT_CALL_DEPTH is for linux kernel text, and INCREMENT_CALL_DEPTH_PKVM is for pkvm text when CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL\u003dy. Of cause, we can also make the implementation as you suggested, then both linux kernel text and pkvm text will use the percpu variable called pcpu_hot__pkvm.call_depth. For pkvm text, this is fine. For the linux kernel, it should also work as the linux kernel also has pcpu_hot__pkvm, but this may not be consistent with the other places where is using pcpu_hot.call_depth, e.g., in retpoline.S call_depth_return_thunk(). And make linux kernel to use the percpu variable called pcpu_hot__pkvm is a bit weird to me. Meanwhile, we don\u0027t want the pkvm text to have CALL_THUNKS_DEBUG_INC_CALLS which is debugging purpose and requires more symbols. So in the end, prefer to separate them.",
